WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.094 --> 00:00:04.541
Summer was coming to an end.

2
00:00:04.542 --> 00:00:08.624
Townspeople continued to gather at the statue.

3
00:00:08.625 --> 00:00:11.276
Some came to admire it.

4
00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:15.207
Others enjoyed its smile.

5
00:00:15.208 --> 00:00:20.749
But most still came to talk about their problems.

6
00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.999
The statue listened to everything they said.

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.251
Hearing people's problems every day was hard.

8
00:00:27.252 --> 00:00:32.749
And it was making him sad.

9
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:38.541
Even compliments about his beauty couldn't make him happy anymore.

10
00:00:38.542 --> 00:00:43.791
"I never knew life was so hard," he thought.

11
00:00:43.792 --> 00:00:54.207
"But now I do. If only I could stop smiling, I could show people that I'm listening to their pain.

12
00:00:54.208 --> 00:01:00.666
But like my heart, my smile is made of heavy stone."

13
00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:05.041
A few days later, Swallow flew over the town.

14
00:01:05.042 --> 00:01:08.957
He was looking for a gift to bring to his love.

15
00:01:08.958 --> 00:01:14.499
"I want something as beautiful as she is," he thought.

16
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.791
He spotted some daisies down on a hilltop.

17
00:01:18.792 --> 00:01:23.291
But they had begun to wilt.

18
00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:28.291
So Swallow flew on until he saw an apple orchard.

19
00:01:28.292 --> 00:01:33.082
"I'll bring her a bright red apple," he thought.

20
00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:38.499
But none of the apples looked right.

21
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.194
At last, Swallow spotted the perfect thing.

22
00:01:42.195 --> 00:01:46.874
A rosebush was growing under a statue.

23
00:01:46.875 --> 00:01:54.291
"Hooray!" Swallow cheered. "I'll pick the most perfect rose!"

24
00:01:54.292 --> 00:01:57.805
Swallow swooped toward the rosebush.

25
00:01:57.806 --> 00:02:02.838
But as he flew past the statue, something flashed in his eye.

26
00:02:02.839 --> 00:02:07.621
It was the statue's gold, gleaming brightly in the sun.

27
00:02:07.622 --> 00:02:13.087
Its three jewels sparkled like stars at night.

28
00:02:13.088 --> 00:02:16.884
Swallow gasped at its beauty.

29
00:02:16.885 --> 00:02:20.957
"This statue would be the finest gift for my love.

30
00:02:20.958 --> 00:02:24.124
If only it wasn't so big and heavy!

31
00:02:24.125 --> 00:02:27.707
Oh well. A perfect rose will do."

32
00:02:27.708 --> 00:02:33.908
Swallow continued toward the roses when he heard a moan.

33
00:02:33.909 --> 00:02:38.749
He looked around but didn't see anyone.

34
00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.712
"Who's there?"

35
00:02:40.713 --> 00:02:47.249
No one answered. There was another moan.

36
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:53.980
It sounded like it was coming from the statue.

37
00:02:53.981 --> 00:02:57.908
"It couldn't be the statue," Swallow thought.

38
00:02:57.909 --> 00:03:03.499
"It looks so happy. And nothing that beautiful could ever be sad.

39
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:11.296
Besides, statues don't talk. Do they? It must have been the wind."

40
00:03:11.297 --> 00:03:18.249
Swallow started looking for the best rose when his flock landed nearby.

41
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:22.804
"Swallow! Come along," Leader called.

42
00:03:22.805 --> 00:03:27.291
"It's time to fly to Egypt."

43
00:03:27.292 --> 00:03:30.124
"Have a good trip," Swallow said.

44
00:03:30.125 --> 00:03:34.004
"I'm staying here, near my love."

45
00:03:34.005 --> 00:03:41.954
Leader frowned. "Winter is coming. You'll freeze."

46
00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:46.666
"I have my love to keep me warm," Swallow said.

47
00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:50.272
"You're making a mistake," Leader said.

48
00:03:50.273 --> 00:03:55.707
"But if you insist, then I wish you good luck."

49
00:03:55.708 --> 00:04:05.382
"I won't need it!" Swallow said as the flock flew away.

